"Constructs": {
  "index": "-100",
  "category": "constructs",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Constructs"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Constructs",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " are humanoid shaped creations that have been imbued with magic in order to give them a semblance of life. Simple constructs can be made from light materials, with the necessary runes being purchased from "
        },
        {
          "text": "Runesmith Villagers",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ", though much stronger and more versatile ones can likely be crafted. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Making the Parts"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Constructs ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "are created from 5 parts: "
        },
        {
          "text": "Head, Torso, Legs, and 2 arms",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": ". "
        },
        {
          "text": "These parts dictate what the construct is capable of.",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\n\nI should take some time to look through the various parts in the Constructs section of the Codex and decide which ones I want to make.\n\nOnce I have decided which parts you want to make, I'll need to decide on a material.\n\nThere are seven materials that a Construct can be made from, and "
        },
        {
          "text": "each changes the properties of the construct",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\n"
        },
        {
          "text": "I can mix and match materials in a single Construct",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and this will balance the benefits and disadvantages of the construct. It will be worthwhile to experiment with different combinations to find one that suits my needs.  "
        },
        {
          "text": "In general, higher tier materials perform tasks faster than lower tier materials, however there are a few exceptions.  I've outlined those where they exist.",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "\n\nI can modify a construct at any time by commanding it to return to an empty "
        },
        {
          "text": "Construct Gantry",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Wickerwood",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Wickerwood ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "construct parts are made from sticks and wheat. They are "
        },
        {
          "text": "buoyant ",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "and "
        },
        {
          "text": "light",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", meaning they help constructs to float and move more quickly. However they cause the construct to "
        },
        {
          "text": "take more damage from fire and burn in the nether",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and they "
        },
        {
          "text": "don't offer much in terms of health",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nWickerwood constructs are also extremely primitive and as such are not capable of more complex tasks or displaying emotion.  The available parts for Wickerwood constructs are limited."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Wood",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Wooden ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "construct parts are made from any kind of wood. They are "
        },
        {
          "text": "buoyant ",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "and "
        },
        {
          "text": "light",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", meaning they help constructs to float and move more quickly. However they cause the construct to take "
        },
        {
          "text": "more damage from fire and burn in the nether",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and they "
        },
        {
          "text": "don't offer much in terms of health",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  They are essentially "
        },
        {
          "text": "a more sturdy version of Wickerwood",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nWooden constructs "
        },
        {
          "text": "regenerate health more quickly",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " than other constructs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Bone",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Bone ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "construct parts are made from bones. Similar to wooden constructs, they are "
        },
        {
          "text": "buoyant ",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "and "
        },
        {
          "text": "light",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", meaning they help constructs to float and move more quickly."
        },
        {
          "text": "Bone constructs have light-medium health and armor",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".  They are essentially "
        },
        {
          "text": "a more sturdy version of Wood",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nBone constructs "
        },
        {
          "text": "regenerate health more quickly",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " than other constructs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Stone",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Stone ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "constructs are more sturdy than wood, though they "
        },
        {
          "text": "will sink in water",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nAs it is a heavier material, constructs with more stone parts are "
        },
        {
          "text": "more resistant to being knocked back",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " by attacks. \n\nStone constructs are "
        },
        {
          "text": "sturdy workers and are mostly generalized",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Iron",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "The primary choice for village golem material, "
        },
        {
          "text": "iron",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": " constructs have seen a significant amount of use. It "
        },
        {
          "text": "sinks quickly and moves slowly, ",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "but "
        },
        {
          "text": "resists being knocked back ",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "and "
        },
        {
          "text": "has significantly more health/armor",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nIron Constructs tend to "
        },
        {
          "text": "specialize in defense and survivability",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Gold",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Gold ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "constructs, similar to iron sink quickly.  They "
        },
        {
          "text": "move faster",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " than their iron counterparts, and their "
        },
        {
          "text": "mana torso has a much higher capacity",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", however they have "
        },
        {
          "text": "much lower health and armor",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " than iron.\n\nGold Constructs tend to "
        },
        {
          "text": "specialize in spell casting tasks",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Obsidian",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Obsidian ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "constructs are somewhat "
        },
        {
          "text": "brittle with only moderate health",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " but deal "
        },
        {
          "text": "extreme amounts of damage",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", higher than any other material.  Their material uniquely can make them "
        },
        {
          "text": "immune to fire and lava",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " provided they have at least 3 obsidian parts.\n\nThey have "
        },
        {
          "text": "low buoyancy",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", but can "
        },
        {
          "text": "move fairly quickly",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ".\n\nObsidian constructs "
        },
        {
          "text": "tend to act in a striker role",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "title",
      "value": "Diamond",
      "newPage": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "json": [
        {
          "text": "Diamond ",
          "color": "blue"
        },
        {
          "text": "constructs are"
        },
        {
          "text": " very resilient",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " and "
        },
        {
          "text": "not overly heavy",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": " in terms of buoyancy. They're "
        },
        {
          "text": "quicker ",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": "too, but offer "
        },
        {
          "text": "no knockback resistance",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ". \n\nDiamond constructs are a "
        },
        {
          "text": "jack-of-all-trades",
          "color": "dark_purple"
        },
        {
          "text": ", excelling at almost any task though not necessarily the best at every task."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "related_recipes": [
    {
      "type": "crafting",
      "location": "mna:bell_of_bidding"
    }
  ]
}